{"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"kind":"symbol","sections":[],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph\/stronglyConnectedComponents()"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity","doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/GraphProtocols","doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph"]]},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/connectivity\/graphprotocols\/directedgraph\/stronglyconnectedcomponents()"]}],"abstract":[{"text":"The strongly connected components: maximal sets of vertices each reaching every other.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Tarjan’s algorithm, iterative, O(V + E).","type":"text"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"stronglyConnectedComponents"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/Components","preciseIdentifier":"s:12Connectivity10ComponentsV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Components"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"anchor":"discussion","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Discussion"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Components are in the order Tarjan’s algorithm completes them, on a depth-first search"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with roots in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" order and successors in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"successors(of:)"},{"type":"text","text":" order (the order of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"NetworkX, petgraph and Boost). That is a reverse topological order of the condensation:"},{"typ